{
  "id": "layers/card-and-registry-name-the-layer",
  "title": "a launch of a user build prints the layer on the card and the registry line records the layer, the real file and the SHA-256 of its bytes; a project build records the layer repo",
  "source": [
    "intended: builds come from layers (repo, trusted parent folders, user folder), nearest wins (docs/decisions.md)"
  ],
  "status": {
    "ts": "xfail",
    "go": "pass"
  },
  "defect": "N-12",
  "intent": "INTENDED behavior (defect N-12, build layers). Every launch line of the registry gains build_layer (repo, parent or user), build_file (the real absolute path of the build file) and build_sha256 (the SHA-256 of the file's bytes, not of anything re-encoded), so a record names exactly which file a session was launched from. The card header of a parent or user build ends with ` (<layer>)`, and card.txt holds the same header; a project build has no suffix. The registry line carries build and build_version (v: 2, defect N-31). The oracle knows no layers: it rejects the user build as an unknown preset and the case FAILS on it.",
  "project": {
    "files": {
      ".jitso/briefs/brief.md": {
        "from": "brief.md"
      }
    }
  },
  "home": {
    "files": {
      ".jitso/builds/shared-scan.yaml": {
        "from": "shared-scan.yaml"
      }
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "run": [
        "launch",
        "--build",
        "shared-scan",
        "--brief",
        "{{PROJECT}}/.jitso/briefs/brief.md",
        "--mode",
        "direct"
      ],
      "capture": {
        "LAUNCH_ID": {
          "from": "stdout",
          "regex": "JITSO (L\\d{8}T\\d{6}-[0-9a-f]{4})",
          "group": 1
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": [
          {
            "contains": "| build shared-scan v1 (user)\n"
          }
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "path": ".jitso/launches/{{LAUNCH_ID}}/card.txt",
            "contains": [
              "| build shared-scan v1 (user)\n"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "registry": {
          "count": 1,
          "events": [
            {
              "at": 0,
              "event": "launch",
              "fields": {
                "build": "shared-scan",
                "build_version": 1,
                "build_layer": "user",
                "build_file": "{{HOME}}/.jitso/builds/shared-scan.yaml",
                "build_sha256": "0d53cd1b501d0f73dc2587f0469a127bbde4c5cdd94eac6691904ededea8a097"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "run": [
        "launch",
        "--build",
        "haiku-explorer",
        "--brief",
        "{{PROJECT}}/.jitso/briefs/brief.md",
        "--mode",
        "direct"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": [
          {
            "regex": "\\| build haiku-explorer v1\\n"
          }
        ],
        "registry": {
          "count": 2,
          "events": [
            {
              "at": 1,
              "event": "launch",
              "fields": {
                "build": "haiku-explorer",
                "build_layer": "repo",
                "build_file": "{{PROJECT}}/jitso/builds/haiku-explorer.yaml",
                "build_sha256": {
                  "regex": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
